job-description-sw-empire-moff = The top Imperial commander on Balmorra. Take tasks from the console, call in artillery and decide where the troops go.
job-description-sw-empire-major = A senior Imperial officer. Take tasks from the console and give orders to lieutenants and soldiers.
job-description-sw-empire-lieutenant = An Imperial field officer. Lead a squad into battle, pass on orders and see that tasks get done.
job-description-sw-empire-soldier = The backbone of the Empire. Follow your officers, hold the factories and bases, destroy Republic troops.
job-description-sw-empire-medic = An Imperial field medic. Stay close to your squad, treat the wounded and keep them alive.
job-description-sw-empire-engineer = An Imperial engineer. Repair structures and machines, keep power and factories running.
job-description-sw-empire-pilot = An Imperial pilot. Operate ships and combat vehicles. You have a jetpack and a mass scanner, but no weapon.
job-description-sw-sith = A dark side Force user with the Imperial army. Lead the attack with a lightsaber and Force powers, seek out Jedi to fight.
job-description-sw-sobrik-captain = The commander of the Sobrik garrison. Hold the city and the roads, give orders to your officers.
job-description-sw-sobrik-officer = A soldier of the Sobrik garrison. Keep the city and the roads under control, do not let the enemy through.
job-description-sw-sobrik-medic = A medic of the Sobrik garrison. Treat the wounded of the garrison and stay close to your people.
job-description-sw-empire-intelligence-caretaker = The head of Imperial Intelligence on Balmorra. Direct your agents and reach targets unseen. The stealth generator turns off when you shoot.
job-description-sw-empire-intelligence-agent = An Imperial Intelligence agent. Reach your target unseen and remove it quietly. The stealth generator turns off when you shoot.
job-description-sw-republic-general = The top Republic commander on Balmorra. Take tasks from the console and decide where the troops go.
job-description-sw-republic-captain = A senior Republic officer. Take tasks from the console and give orders to lieutenants and soldiers.
job-description-sw-republic-lieutenant = A Republic field officer. Lead a squad into battle, pass on orders and see that tasks get done.
job-description-sw-republic-soldier = The backbone of the Republic. Follow your officers, take back the factories and bases, destroy Imperial troops.
job-description-sw-republic-recruit = A new Republic recruit. Stay close to the soldiers, follow your officers and learn as you go.
job-description-sw-republic-medic = A Republic field medic. Stay close to your squad, treat the wounded and keep them alive.
job-description-sw-republic-engineer = A Republic engineer. Repair structures and machines, keep power and factories running.
job-description-sw-republic-pilot = A Republic pilot. Operate ships and combat vehicles. You have a jetpack and a mass scanner, but no weapon.
job-description-sw-jedi = A light side Force user with the Republic army. Protect people with a lightsaber and Force powers, hold back the Sith.
job-description-sw-havok-commander = The commander of the Havok special forces squad. Take the hardest tasks and lead the squad where regular troops cannot go.
job-description-sw-havok-lieutenant = The second in command of Havok. Lead part of the squad, pass on orders and take over if the commander falls.
job-description-sw-havok-medic = The medic of Havok. Move with the squad and treat its fighters in the middle of battle.
job-description-sw-havok-stormtrooper = A Havok assault trooper. Go in first and break enemy defences with a heavy weapon.
job-description-sw-havok-sniper = The Havok sniper. Take a position and pick off officers and key targets from afar.
job-description-sw-mandalorian-leader = The leader of the Mandalorian band, an independent side. Take tasks from the console: beast hunts, bounties, money and documents.
job-description-sw-mandalorian-veteran = An experienced Mandalorian warrior. Help the leader finish tasks and look for a worthy fight.
job-description-sw-mandalorian-warrior = A Mandalorian warrior. You serve neither the Empire nor the Republic: finish the band's tasks and fight for honour and pay.
job-description-sw-mandalorian-recruit = A newcomer among the Mandalorians. Stay with your elders, finish the band's tasks and prove you are a warrior.
job-description-sw-black-sun-captain = The head of a Black Sun syndicate cell. Take contracts from the console: killings, raids and loot. You may be declared wanted.
job-description-sw-black-sun-mercenary = A Black Sun mercenary. Carry out the captain's contracts for money and do not get caught. You may be declared wanted.
job-description-sw-exchange-captain = The head of an Exchange cell. Take contracts from the console and profit from someone else's war. You may be declared wanted.
job-description-sw-exchange-operative = An Exchange operative. Carry out the captain's contracts and protect the cell's business. You may be declared wanted.
job-description-sw-civilian = A resident of Balmorra caught between two armies. You have no faction, radio or weapon: find work, trade and try to survive.
job-description-sw-bartender = The owner of the bar. Serve food and drinks to anyone who comes in. You take no side; the pistol in your pocket is just in case.
